## Setting Up Storybook

Storybook 8.x has good Svelte 5 + SvelteKit support. Here's how to set it up:

### 1. Install Storybook

Run this in your project root:

```clubatime/terminal#L1
pnpm dlx storybook@latest init --type sveltekit
```

This will:
- Detect your SvelteKit setup
- Install the right dependencies (`@storybook/sveltekit`, `@storybook/svelte`, etc.)
- Create `.storybook/` config folder
- Add example stories

### 2. After Installation

You'll get these new files:

```/dev/null/structure.txt#L1-5
.storybook/
├── main.ts       # Storybook config
├── preview.ts    # Global decorators, CSS imports
src/stories/      # Example stories (you can delete these later)
```

### 3. Import Your Global CSS

Update `.storybook/preview.ts` to include your app styles:

```/dev/null/.storybook/preview.ts#L1-12
import type { Preview } from '@storybook/svelte';
import '../src/lib/styles/app.css';

const preview: Preview = {
  parameters: {
    backgrounds: {
      default: 'dark',
      values: [
        { name: 'dark', value: '#17171d' },
        { name: 'light', value: '#ffffff' },
      ],
    },
  },
};

export default preview;
```

### 4. Run Storybook

```clubatime/terminal#L1
pnpm storybook
```

This opens Storybook at `http://localhost:6006`.

